A33 — blank the output on the session-end path

The reaper (A27/A28) ends the session when the game's process is gone, but wine's
virtual desktop window outlives the game: by then it is the compositor's only
remaining client, so the last commit -- and what the display is left holding --
is wine's desktop background. The compositor already waits on the reaper's exit
to end the session; hold the output black there, and paint one black frame
before the loop stops.

The same desktop background is what the panel is left holding at the other end:
from startup until the guest's first frame arrives on the override surface,
wine's desktop is the only window the compositor has. So the blank is raised on
the texture selection itself -- is this window's newest done commit still the
override surface's? -- and not on the reaper alone, and a window that has never
had an override surface is never blanked.

